// Version Control & Asset Management: I managed the synchronization of technical assets and their corresponding metadata files
 (.meta). I ensured that scripts like ControlEntradaSalida were correctly serialized within the 
Unity environment, maintaining the integrity of the unique
 Global Identifiers (GUIDs) to prevent broken references during collaborative development.
Component Integration: I configured the MonoImporter settings for the project's scripts, ensuring the correct execution order and default references.
 This was crucial for the "Mario Lava Game"
 to recognize player interactions without loss of data between sessions or repository updates.
Environment Logic Setup: Using the Unity Inspector,
 I linked the C# logic with the 3D environment, assigning the 
"Player" tag to the character prefabs so the entry/exit triggers would function as planned in the game's architecture.
